# ==========================================
# Security Policy with Conflicting & Shadowed Rules
# Used to demonstrate Phase 4 (Rule Analysis) & Phase 5 (Optimization: dead-rule elimination)
# ==========================================

# Rule 1: Allow all web traffic on port 80
RULE ALLOW_HTTP_ANY
WHEN TCP PORT 80
IF SOURCE ANY
THEN ALLOW

# Rule 2: Conflicting rule with opposite action for the exact same condition
# Under first-match semantics, this rule will NEVER trigger!
RULE BLOCK_HTTP_ANY
WHEN TCP PORT 80
IF SOURCE ANY
THEN BLOCK

# Rule 3: Broad rule blocking all external traffic
RULE BLOCK_ALL_EXTERNAL
WHEN ANY PORT ANY
IF SOURCE EXTERNAL
THEN BLOCK

# Rule 4: Narrower rule attempting to allow external HTTPS
# Because Rule 3 precedes this and matches all EXTERNAL traffic with BLOCK,
# Rule 4 is completely shadowed and can never execute!
RULE ALLOW_EXTERNAL_HTTPS
WHEN TCP PORT 443
IF SOURCE EXTERNAL
THEN ALLOW
